1
00:00:25,759 --> 00:00:27,959
♪ ♪

2
00:00:36,470 --> 00:00:38,137
♪ ♪

3
00:00:49,216 --> 00:00:51,250
♪ ♪

4
00:01:04,565 --> 00:01:06,276
<i>It was pouring.</i>

5
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:08,800
<i>We skidded out of control.</i>

6
00:01:21,381 --> 00:01:23,281
<i>I couldn't see Dora.</i>

7
00:01:23,350 --> 00:01:25,783
<i>I didn't know where she was.</i>

8
00:01:37,831 --> 00:01:41,666
<i>Somehow, I got
myself out of the car.</i>

9
00:01:48,542 --> 00:01:51,476
♪ ♪

10
00:02:10,063 --> 00:02:11,996
♪ ♪

11
00:02:20,307 --> 00:02:23,007
<i>There was nothing I could do.</i>

12
00:02:23,076 --> 00:02:26,878
<i>Nothing I could
do; I was helpless.</i>

13
00:02:36,657 --> 00:02:39,424
<i>If Dora hadn't... been there...</i>

14
00:02:47,067 --> 00:02:49,045
You'd have burned to death,

15
00:02:49,069 --> 00:02:52,036
as your dog did.

16
00:02:52,105 --> 00:02:55,240
It's been two years since...

17
00:02:55,309 --> 00:02:56,309
Can you say it?

18
00:02:57,977 --> 00:02:59,744
Since the fire, Erin.

19
00:03:03,283 --> 00:03:05,783
Why am I dreaming about it now?

20
00:03:05,852 --> 00:03:07,452
What's happening now?

21
00:03:07,521 --> 00:03:10,322
What's frightening you,
making you feel helpless?

22
00:03:11,791 --> 00:03:14,626
You think I'm having
the nightmares

23
00:03:14,695 --> 00:03:17,161
because I decided
to divorce Adam?

24
00:03:17,231 --> 00:03:19,364
What I think doesn't matter.

25
00:03:19,433 --> 00:03:20,865
What do you think?

26
00:03:20,934 --> 00:03:23,335
Do you think there
could be a connection?

27
00:03:26,139 --> 00:03:28,473
Of course there's a connection.

28
00:03:28,542 --> 00:03:30,475
You're angry.

29
00:03:31,578 --> 00:03:33,445
I'll see you next Thursday.

30
00:03:33,513 --> 00:03:35,358
You're upset, Erin;
let's talk about this.

31
00:03:35,382 --> 00:03:36,481
Thursday.

32
00:03:36,550 --> 00:03:39,417
Erin, if the idea
of divorcing Adam

33
00:03:39,486 --> 00:03:41,553
is upsetting you this
much, you can wait,

34
00:03:41,622 --> 00:03:43,355
you don't have to do it now.

35
00:03:45,859 --> 00:03:47,859
Yes, I do.

36
00:04:21,128 --> 00:04:23,294
Adam, we have to talk.

37
00:04:23,363 --> 00:04:25,430
I'm sorry, uh...

38
00:04:25,499 --> 00:04:27,265
I'm expecting Hillary Benson.

39
00:04:27,334 --> 00:04:29,134
We'll talk after our meeting.

40
00:04:30,404 --> 00:04:32,904
Adam, I... I want a divorce.

41
00:04:37,444 --> 00:04:38,809
Oh.

42
00:04:38,878 --> 00:04:40,045
I see.

43
00:04:48,088 --> 00:04:52,524
Well... let's, uh...

44
00:04:52,592 --> 00:04:55,260
let's suppose I don't
stand in your way.

45
00:04:55,328 --> 00:04:57,462
Where will you go?

46
00:04:57,531 --> 00:04:59,130
What will you do?

47
00:04:59,199 --> 00:05:01,132
I-I'll manage.

48
00:05:01,201 --> 00:05:03,101
Alone?

49
00:05:03,170 --> 00:05:05,137
You will be alone, you know.

50
00:05:05,205 --> 00:05:07,606
Yes.

51
00:05:07,674 --> 00:05:13,011
Without my loving care,
my... financial support.

52
00:05:13,079 --> 00:05:15,747
I have lawyers who
will make certain

53
00:05:15,815 --> 00:05:18,883
you will be without
my financial support.

54
00:05:20,954 --> 00:05:22,854
Look at you.

55
00:05:22,922 --> 00:05:25,390
You're a cripple.

56
00:05:25,459 --> 00:05:28,126
You're weak.

57
00:05:28,195 --> 00:05:30,562
You can't survive without me.

58
00:05:30,631 --> 00:05:34,432
All right, stop it,
stop your crying.

59
00:05:36,102 --> 00:05:37,469
Erin!

60
00:05:38,805 --> 00:05:41,005
There will not be a divorce.

61
00:05:41,074 --> 00:05:45,310
You will never,
<i>never</i> get rid of me.

62
00:05:45,379 --> 00:05:47,845
Do you understand?

63
00:05:53,287 --> 00:05:55,387
Dr. Forbes is behind this.

64
00:05:56,556 --> 00:05:58,589
My diary! Give that to me!

65
00:05:58,658 --> 00:06:00,392
It's all in here, Erin!

66
00:06:00,460 --> 00:06:02,060
Forbes is your lover!

67
00:06:02,129 --> 00:06:03,361
Oh, that's not true!

68
00:06:03,430 --> 00:06:04,529
Oh, yes, it is.

69
00:06:04,597 --> 00:06:06,998
He's urged you to divorce me.

70
00:06:07,067 --> 00:06:08,900
Well, the Medical Review Board

71
00:06:08,968 --> 00:06:11,580
will take away his license
for that. How dare you

72
00:06:11,604 --> 00:06:13,171
try to stop Dr. Forbes!

73
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:14,606
I'll do more than that.

74
00:06:14,675 --> 00:06:16,374
I'll ruin him.

75
00:06:16,442 --> 00:06:20,178
Lovers! A doctor
without a license,

76
00:06:20,247 --> 00:06:21,479
and a cripple!

77
00:06:21,548 --> 00:06:24,315
Oh, that's... nice.

78
00:06:31,691 --> 00:06:33,591
Hillary, come in.

79
00:06:34,661 --> 00:06:36,994
Uh, Mrs. Whitley is tired.

80
00:06:37,063 --> 00:06:39,497
Would you please
take her upstairs?

81
00:06:51,578 --> 00:06:53,811
You wanted to see me, Adam?

82
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:57,782
Yes. There's been
a... change in plans.

83
00:07:00,286 --> 00:07:01,486
It's hopeless.

84
00:07:01,555 --> 00:07:04,823
I... I don't want to
live like this anymore.

85
00:07:07,594 --> 00:07:10,528
Take this and you'll sleep.

86
00:07:10,597 --> 00:07:12,564
Then what?

87
00:07:12,632 --> 00:07:14,899
I'll just have to wake up again.

88
00:07:31,017 --> 00:07:33,563
Things will look
better in the morning.

89
00:07:33,587 --> 00:07:37,522
No. It's no use.

90
00:07:54,107 --> 00:07:55,684
You can't do this to me, Adam!

91
00:07:55,708 --> 00:07:56,752
I already have!

92
00:07:56,776 --> 00:07:58,388
Now, if it isn't
too much trouble,

93
00:07:58,412 --> 00:08:00,972
will you see yourself out!

94
00:08:14,628 --> 00:08:16,427
It's Dr. Forbes, Mr. Whitley.

95
00:08:16,496 --> 00:08:19,264
Mrs. Whitley called
me... It's an emergency.

96
00:08:19,333 --> 00:08:22,734
Hers or yours, Dr. Forbes?

97
00:08:22,802 --> 00:08:24,902
Go ahead.

98
00:08:41,054 --> 00:08:43,454
What the hell do you want now?

99
00:09:22,429 --> 00:09:24,930
Now, you told the
arresting officer

100
00:09:24,998 --> 00:09:27,799
you arrived at the
house at 10:00?

101
00:09:27,867 --> 00:09:29,301
Yes.

102
00:09:29,369 --> 00:09:32,748
My radio was on... the 10:00
news was just coming on.

103
00:09:32,772 --> 00:09:34,172
Uh-huh, uh-huh.

104
00:09:34,241 --> 00:09:37,242
And-and the police
got their call at 10:10.

105
00:09:37,311 --> 00:09:38,609
Did you call 'em?

106
00:09:38,678 --> 00:09:40,845
No, I didn't.

107
00:09:40,914 --> 00:09:43,781
Well, Mrs. Whitley's,
uh, companion, Dora,

108
00:09:43,850 --> 00:09:47,986
uh, said that when she saw you,
you were running up the stairs.

109
00:09:48,055 --> 00:09:50,055
What were you gonna do?

110
00:09:50,123 --> 00:09:52,857
Well, I was going
to find my patient.

111
00:09:52,926 --> 00:09:56,194
Isn't it unusual for a
psychiatrist to make house calls?

112
00:09:56,263 --> 00:10:00,898
It's highly unusual,
but Erin had called me,

113
00:10:00,968 --> 00:10:04,202
sounding distraught and,
in my opinion, suicidal.

114
00:10:04,271 --> 00:10:05,903
Had she done it before?

115
00:10:05,973 --> 00:10:08,440
Mm-mm, never, but...

116
00:10:08,508 --> 00:10:12,777
her conflicts are severe enough
to cause hysterical paralysis.

117
00:10:12,846 --> 00:10:14,379
Hysterical paralysis?

118
00:10:14,448 --> 00:10:16,514
It means it's
psychologically caused

119
00:10:16,583 --> 00:10:18,816
but nonetheless very real.

120
00:10:18,885 --> 00:10:21,619
I mean, so real
that two years ago,

121
00:10:21,688 --> 00:10:24,022
in a fire, she
suffered severe burns,

122
00:10:24,091 --> 00:10:25,423
and she nearly died

123
00:10:25,492 --> 00:10:28,159
because she
couldn't save herself.

124
00:10:28,228 --> 00:10:30,106
She was suffering
hysterical paralysis then.

125
00:10:30,130 --> 00:10:31,863
Oh.

126
00:10:31,931 --> 00:10:33,631
Mm, mm.

127
00:10:34,968 --> 00:10:39,170
Well... how did, um...

128
00:10:39,239 --> 00:10:42,040
how did she, uh, get
along with her husband?

129
00:10:42,109 --> 00:10:45,042
She was planning to
ask him for a divorce.

130
00:10:45,112 --> 00:10:46,978
Oh.

131
00:10:47,046 --> 00:10:50,147
Maybe they argued,
and<i> she</i> killed him.

132
00:10:50,216 --> 00:10:51,849
No.

133
00:10:51,918 --> 00:10:54,585
Erin is psychologically
and physically

134
00:10:54,654 --> 00:10:56,620
incapable of killing anyone.

135
00:10:56,690 --> 00:10:57,955
In your opinion.

136
00:10:58,025 --> 00:10:59,257
In fact.

137
00:11:02,095 --> 00:11:03,527
Oh.

138
00:11:10,503 --> 00:11:11,803
Lawyer's office.

139
00:11:11,871 --> 00:11:13,216
Benjamin Matlock?

140
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:14,672
Yes, this is Ben Matlock.

141
00:11:14,741 --> 00:11:17,542
There's something
important you should know.

142
00:11:17,611 --> 00:11:19,110
Who is this?

143
00:11:19,178 --> 00:11:22,046
Dr. Forbes and Erin
Whitley are lovers.

144
00:11:22,115 --> 00:11:24,549
Dr. Forbes killed Adam Whitley.

145
00:11:25,686 --> 00:11:27,886
Who is this?

146
00:11:27,954 --> 00:11:31,455
Never mind who I am.

147
00:11:31,524 --> 00:11:34,826
Just ask Dr. Forbes
about Erin's diary.

148
00:11:34,895 --> 00:11:36,260
What diary?

149
00:11:38,331 --> 00:11:40,098
Hello?

150
00:11:40,167 --> 00:11:41,465
Hello?

151
00:11:44,337 --> 00:11:46,004
Huh.

152
00:11:50,643 --> 00:11:52,943
I was in my room down the hall.

153
00:11:53,012 --> 00:11:55,524
And you didn't hear the shots?

154
00:11:55,548 --> 00:11:58,449
No. I told the police I
was wearing headphones.

155
00:11:58,518 --> 00:11:59,950
I was doing leg lifts.

156
00:12:00,019 --> 00:12:01,252
How's that?

157
00:12:01,320 --> 00:12:03,532
I was exercising
to a workout tape.

158
00:12:03,556 --> 00:12:04,734
Hips.

159
00:12:04,758 --> 00:12:06,624
Oh.

160
00:12:06,693 --> 00:12:08,593
Now, why did you
come downstairs?

161
00:12:08,661 --> 00:12:10,862
I saw a light on.

162
00:12:10,930 --> 00:12:15,466
And, uh, uh, Mr. Whitley
was, uh, where?

163
00:12:15,535 --> 00:12:18,536
Right there.

164
00:12:18,605 --> 00:12:20,237
What else did you see?

165
00:12:20,306 --> 00:12:21,684
I saw Dr. Forbes
running up the stairs.

166
00:12:21,708 --> 00:12:22,807
Oh. You know him?

167
00:12:22,876 --> 00:12:25,020
No. Mrs. Whitley
has talked about him,

168
00:12:25,044 --> 00:12:26,389
but I'd never seen him before.

169
00:12:26,413 --> 00:12:28,679
And you don't know
who called the police?

170
00:12:28,748 --> 00:12:30,615
No.

171
00:12:30,683 --> 00:12:32,517
Could it have been Mrs. Whitley?

172
00:12:32,585 --> 00:12:34,597
No. She had taken
her sleeping pill.

173
00:12:34,621 --> 00:12:36,265
I had given it to her myself.

174
00:12:36,289 --> 00:12:39,157
And later, when the police
had asked me to wake her,

175
00:12:39,226 --> 00:12:40,369
it took me five minutes

176
00:12:40,393 --> 00:12:42,138
and even then, she
was too groggy to talk,

177
00:12:42,162 --> 00:12:43,894
never mind answer questions.

178
00:12:45,732 --> 00:12:48,866
I appreciate your
time, Mrs. Whitley,

179
00:12:48,935 --> 00:12:51,101
and I'll be as
brief as possible.

180
00:12:51,170 --> 00:12:55,205
Um, I understand you were
asleep when your husband was killed

181
00:12:55,274 --> 00:12:57,542
and you did not hear the shots.

182
00:12:57,610 --> 00:13:00,611
Yes, it was a
sleeping pill night.

183
00:13:00,680 --> 00:13:02,413
I heard nothing.

184
00:13:02,481 --> 00:13:04,481
And when Miss Marquez woke you,

185
00:13:04,551 --> 00:13:08,419
and told you, you... Shocked.

186
00:13:08,487 --> 00:13:12,389
I didn't feel sad.

187
00:13:12,458 --> 00:13:14,391
I wanted to leave him.

188
00:13:14,460 --> 00:13:16,961
I won't pretend that I feel sad.

189
00:13:17,030 --> 00:13:18,829
Mind telling me why?

190
00:13:18,898 --> 00:13:20,431
Why what?

191
00:13:20,499 --> 00:13:21,966
You wanted to leave him.

192
00:13:25,271 --> 00:13:27,538
He used to taunt me.

193
00:13:27,607 --> 00:13:31,241
Say that I was
helpless and weak.

194
00:13:31,310 --> 00:13:34,378
But that's the way
he wanted me to be,

195
00:13:34,447 --> 00:13:37,347
because, if I was
weak and helpless,

196
00:13:37,416 --> 00:13:41,351
then he could feel
stronger and more in control.

197
00:13:41,420 --> 00:13:43,020
Did Dr. Forbes tell you that?

198
00:13:43,089 --> 00:13:44,889
Dr. Forbes helped me to see it

199
00:13:44,958 --> 00:13:48,292
and to see that
having a handicap

200
00:13:48,360 --> 00:13:51,062
isn't the same
thing as being weak.

201
00:13:51,130 --> 00:13:53,297
My husband

202
00:13:53,365 --> 00:13:56,300
might have been seeing
another woman, Mr. Matlock.

203
00:13:56,368 --> 00:13:59,837
Could it be the lady
who visited that evening?

204
00:13:59,906 --> 00:14:01,450
Um, um, um... Hillary Benson?

205
00:14:01,474 --> 00:14:02,573
No.

206
00:14:02,642 --> 00:14:07,612
Their relationship
was strictly business.

207
00:14:10,449 --> 00:14:12,750
Everything's so cloudy.

208
00:14:12,819 --> 00:14:17,521
Dora told me that-that
Adam was getting phone calls

209
00:14:17,590 --> 00:14:21,169
- from a woman named...
- Shannon.

210
00:14:21,193 --> 00:14:23,506
That was the name the woman
left on the answering machine.

211
00:14:23,530 --> 00:14:24,629
Shannon?

212
00:14:24,698 --> 00:14:28,633
Uh, did you ever
talk to this Shannon?

213
00:14:28,702 --> 00:14:31,802
No.

214
00:14:31,871 --> 00:14:35,072
I don't think so.

215
00:14:35,141 --> 00:14:37,875
No, uh... No,

216
00:14:37,944 --> 00:14:39,888
I never did. I'm
sorry, Mr. Matlock.

217
00:14:39,912 --> 00:14:42,613
Everything is so
confusing lately.

218
00:14:42,682 --> 00:14:44,715
It's my memory. I mean,
a whole day can go by

219
00:14:44,784 --> 00:14:47,151
and I-I don't remember
a single minute of it.

220
00:14:47,220 --> 00:14:49,687
Karen, you're just tired.

221
00:14:49,755 --> 00:14:51,255
Well, um, I'll be going.

222
00:14:51,324 --> 00:14:53,224
No, don't.

223
00:14:53,293 --> 00:14:55,360
I want to do anything I can.

224
00:14:55,428 --> 00:14:57,095
I want to help Dr. Forbes.

225
00:14:57,163 --> 00:15:00,198
You came to see him

226
00:15:00,266 --> 00:15:03,968
after you were burned in a fire?

227
00:15:13,946 --> 00:15:16,280
Yes.

228
00:15:16,349 --> 00:15:17,426
He's helped me a great deal.

229
00:15:17,450 --> 00:15:20,551
Do you keep a diary?

230
00:15:20,620 --> 00:15:22,553
Yes, I do.

231
00:15:22,622 --> 00:15:23,765
Is there anything in it

232
00:15:23,789 --> 00:15:27,425
that would, uh, help
Dr. Forbes' case?

233
00:15:27,494 --> 00:15:31,795
It's just a journal of my
dreams and feelings.

234
00:15:33,633 --> 00:15:35,966
Last time I saw it, Adam
took it out of his drawer

235
00:15:36,036 --> 00:15:38,036
in his library. He did?

236
00:15:40,040 --> 00:15:42,240
It was very upsetting.

237
00:15:44,110 --> 00:15:46,044
I'm sure.

238
00:15:58,124 --> 00:16:00,057
♪ ♪

239
00:16:15,341 --> 00:16:17,274
Yeah.

240
00:16:26,419 --> 00:16:29,854
Tyler, I got somebody
I want you to check out.

241
00:16:32,057 --> 00:16:35,097
<i>You're sure you've cleared
this with Miss Blackwell?</i>

242
00:16:36,996 --> 00:16:40,398
Look, when she applied
for our insurance...

243
00:16:40,467 --> 00:16:42,667
she gave us permission
to inspect the premises.

244
00:16:44,337 --> 00:16:45,481
I don't understand this.

245
00:16:45,505 --> 00:16:48,406
She looked so neat.

246
00:16:48,475 --> 00:16:50,774
Well, somebody was
obviously looking for something.

247
00:16:57,750 --> 00:17:00,084
Mr. Putnam, do you ever recall

248
00:17:00,153 --> 00:17:02,487
Miss Blackwell seeing a
middle-aged gentleman

249
00:17:02,555 --> 00:17:04,155
by the name of Adam Whitley?

250
00:17:04,224 --> 00:17:05,504
Can't say that I do.

251
00:17:07,160 --> 00:17:09,604
I don't know any of her friends.

252
00:17:09,628 --> 00:17:12,229
But I have seen her in the
neighborhood cocktail lounge.

253
00:17:12,298 --> 00:17:13,864
Durand's.

254
00:17:13,933 --> 00:17:15,933
Where's your badge?

255
00:17:16,002 --> 00:17:17,435
I'm not a cop.

256
00:17:17,503 --> 00:17:19,603
Yeah, and I'm not a bartender.

257
00:17:19,672 --> 00:17:22,906
Okay, I've seen her around,
but that's all I can tell you.

258
00:17:22,976 --> 00:17:25,376
Well, I'll tell you.

259
00:17:27,113 --> 00:17:31,315
If she comes back in here
again, have her call that number.

260
00:17:33,152 --> 00:17:34,418
Why not?

261
00:17:34,487 --> 00:17:36,720
Matlock, huh?

262
00:17:36,789 --> 00:17:39,156
Sure sounds like a cop's name.

263
00:17:44,330 --> 00:17:47,331
Well, Hillary Benson lied to me.

264
00:17:47,400 --> 00:17:48,699
What's this?

265
00:17:48,767 --> 00:17:52,403
Galley proofs for <i>Elegance
Magazine's</i> fall issue.

266
00:17:52,472 --> 00:17:54,783
A college chum of mine
is an associate editor.

267
00:17:54,807 --> 00:17:56,273
Hmm.

268
00:17:56,342 --> 00:17:58,753
She said Adam Whitley
was featuring her designs

269
00:17:58,777 --> 00:18:00,055
in his fall issue.

270
00:18:00,079 --> 00:18:03,447
She even had mock-ups made
for an expensive ad campaign

271
00:18:03,516 --> 00:18:04,659
based on his promise.

272
00:18:04,683 --> 00:18:05,883
Mm-hmm.

273
00:18:05,951 --> 00:18:09,120
But, Hillary Benson's
not in the fall issue.

274
00:18:09,188 --> 00:18:11,322
Oh. Adam Whitley dumped her.

275
00:18:11,391 --> 00:18:12,490
Oh.

276
00:18:15,561 --> 00:18:16,660
Hello?

277
00:18:16,729 --> 00:18:18,240
Mr. Matlock.

278
00:18:18,264 --> 00:18:19,696
This is Shannon Blackwell.

279
00:18:19,765 --> 00:18:21,465
I got your message.

280
00:18:21,534 --> 00:18:23,367
Uh, where are you?

281
00:18:23,436 --> 00:18:25,402
Meet me tonight at 11:00.

282
00:18:25,472 --> 00:18:27,271
Where?

283
00:18:27,340 --> 00:18:28,918
There's a dead
end off the parkway

284
00:18:28,942 --> 00:18:30,741
at Junction 18 outside Monroe.

285
00:18:30,810 --> 00:18:31,943
I'll find it.

286
00:18:32,011 --> 00:18:33,077
Come alone.

287
00:18:33,146 --> 00:18:36,513
Sorry for the
inconvenience, Mr. Matlock.

288
00:18:36,582 --> 00:18:38,515
But my life is in danger.

289
00:18:47,727 --> 00:18:49,292
Mr. Matlock.

290
00:18:49,361 --> 00:18:51,294
Yeah.

291
00:18:57,870 --> 00:18:59,803
I'm alone.

292
00:18:59,872 --> 00:19:01,038
I appreciate this.

293
00:19:01,106 --> 00:19:03,051
Your life's in danger?

294
00:19:03,075 --> 00:19:04,307
Let me start at the beginning.

295
00:19:04,376 --> 00:19:05,976
I met Adam Whitley
when I interviewed

296
00:19:06,045 --> 00:19:08,078
for a modeling
assignment for<i> Elegance.</i>

297
00:19:08,147 --> 00:19:12,416
I wasn't right for the magazine,
but I was perfect for Adam.

298
00:19:12,484 --> 00:19:15,886
Well, you were,
um... uh, his mistress?

299
00:19:15,955 --> 00:19:19,690
We were lovers.

300
00:19:19,759 --> 00:19:24,528
Adam paid for my apartment,
my clothes and my car, yes.

301
00:19:24,597 --> 00:19:25,996
I was his mistress.

302
00:19:26,065 --> 00:19:28,265
And you didn't want that.

303
00:19:28,333 --> 00:19:29,934
I must have. I did it.

304
00:19:31,236 --> 00:19:33,114
I was a good model.
I made a good living.

305
00:19:33,138 --> 00:19:35,138
But once I met
Adam, that was that.

306
00:19:35,207 --> 00:19:36,985
He didn't want me
to work, so I didn't.

307
00:19:37,009 --> 00:19:39,176
I lived for him.

308
00:19:39,244 --> 00:19:42,145
Not very smart, I know.

309
00:19:42,214 --> 00:19:43,380
But I loved him

310
00:19:43,449 --> 00:19:46,083
and I thought that if
I loved him enough,

311
00:19:46,151 --> 00:19:49,119
if I was patient enough...

312
00:19:49,188 --> 00:19:50,654
I wanted to marry him.

313
00:19:50,723 --> 00:19:52,656
I see. But now it's too late.

314
00:19:52,725 --> 00:19:55,258
I'm alone and I am in danger.

315
00:19:55,327 --> 00:19:58,562
It was you who called
the other night, wasn't it?

316
00:20:00,132 --> 00:20:02,044
What's in that diary?

317
00:20:02,068 --> 00:20:05,135
Everything.

318
00:20:05,204 --> 00:20:07,471
Erin's affair with Dr. Forbes,

319
00:20:07,539 --> 00:20:09,607
Dr. Forbes' intention
to murder Adam.

320
00:20:09,675 --> 00:20:12,442
Adam intended to use
the diary to divorce Erin

321
00:20:12,511 --> 00:20:14,144
and ruin Forbes' career.

322
00:20:14,213 --> 00:20:16,714
And now, I am next.

323
00:20:16,782 --> 00:20:19,316
My apartment has been
ransacked, Mr. Matlock.

324
00:20:22,154 --> 00:20:26,690
Um... I'm sorry.

325
00:20:26,759 --> 00:20:30,560
But I know that Erin
is trying to kill me.

326
00:20:30,630 --> 00:20:34,031
She is not the innocent that
she pretends to be, Mr. Matlock.

327
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:35,198
You've got to help me.

328
00:20:35,267 --> 00:20:38,368
I don't want to ruin
Erin or Dr. Forbes.

329
00:20:38,437 --> 00:20:39,870
I just want to leave town

330
00:20:39,939 --> 00:20:41,972
and forget that this part
of my life ever happened.

331
00:20:52,017 --> 00:20:54,177
Good morning! MATLOCK: Hey!

332
00:20:59,024 --> 00:21:01,236
How was your meeting
with Shannon Blackwell?

333
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:03,761
Uh, she's kind of weird.

334
00:21:03,829 --> 00:21:06,897
Like Ernie Ford used to say...

335
00:21:06,965 --> 00:21:08,632
She's as nervous
as a long-tailed cat

336
00:21:08,701 --> 00:21:10,233
in a room full of
rocking chairs.

337
00:21:11,470 --> 00:21:14,104
What are you doing?

338
00:21:14,172 --> 00:21:15,572
Oh, it's makeup.

339
00:21:15,641 --> 00:21:17,808
Car came by and scared her

340
00:21:17,877 --> 00:21:19,610
and she damned
near jumped in my lap.

341
00:21:19,678 --> 00:21:20,958
Oh...

342
00:21:21,013 --> 00:21:22,957
Well, you've got to
take that to the cleaners.

343
00:21:22,981 --> 00:21:25,282
Yeah. Hmm.

344
00:21:25,350 --> 00:21:26,750
Well...

345
00:21:26,819 --> 00:21:32,122
She told me there's
something in, uh, Erin's diary

346
00:21:32,190 --> 00:21:36,026
that could, uh,
incriminate our client.

347
00:21:36,094 --> 00:21:39,241
Hillary Benson
mentioned the diary. Yeah.

348
00:21:39,265 --> 00:21:42,433
Everybody's
mentioned that diary.

349
00:21:42,502 --> 00:21:45,469
Except the one person
who should be mentioning it.

350
00:21:47,973 --> 00:21:49,473
I would have
come to your office.

351
00:21:49,542 --> 00:21:52,102
Well, I've never
been to your office.

352
00:21:53,879 --> 00:21:56,439
I spoke to Erin Whitley.

353
00:21:58,451 --> 00:22:01,011
What kind of medication
does she take?

354
00:22:02,221 --> 00:22:04,355
Well, she takes a sleeping pill.

355
00:22:04,424 --> 00:22:05,756
Occasionally, but not nightly.

356
00:22:05,825 --> 00:22:09,125
Would it cause her to
have memory lapses

357
00:22:09,194 --> 00:22:10,354
or forget where she'd been?

358
00:22:12,531 --> 00:22:14,998
Erin told you she was
losing track of time?

359
00:22:15,067 --> 00:22:17,033
Something like that.

360
00:22:17,102 --> 00:22:19,703
She hasn't said
anything about it to me.

361
00:22:19,772 --> 00:22:21,705
She hasn't?

362
00:22:23,576 --> 00:22:26,009
I tell you something

363
00:22:26,078 --> 00:22:27,856
you haven't said
anything about to me.

364
00:22:27,880 --> 00:22:30,213
What's that?

365
00:22:30,282 --> 00:22:31,682
Erin's diary.

366
00:22:31,751 --> 00:22:35,285
Perhaps the most crucial piece
of evidence in the whole case

367
00:22:35,354 --> 00:22:36,832
and you haven't
even mentioned it.

368
00:22:36,856 --> 00:22:38,689
I didn't think it was relevant.

369
00:22:38,758 --> 00:22:43,627
People I've talked to
say, it could convict you.

370
00:22:43,696 --> 00:22:46,096
That's absolutely not true. I...

371
00:22:47,400 --> 00:22:49,966
I read Erin's diary
each month, carefully.

372
00:22:50,035 --> 00:22:51,955
Writing it is part
of her therapy.

373
00:22:52,004 --> 00:22:54,772
It contains nothing that
would be harmful to me.

374
00:22:54,840 --> 00:22:55,906
You've read it?

375
00:22:55,974 --> 00:22:57,841
As recently as ten days ago.

376
00:22:57,910 --> 00:22:59,910
Oh.

377
00:22:59,978 --> 00:23:04,047
Well, you know we'll have
to discuss this diary in court.

378
00:23:05,584 --> 00:23:06,650
I can't.

379
00:23:06,719 --> 00:23:09,286
Patient confidentiality.

380
00:23:09,354 --> 00:23:12,322
I cannot discuss this in court.

381
00:23:12,391 --> 00:23:16,493
Dr. Forbes, I have
knowledge of this diary.

382
00:23:16,562 --> 00:23:20,864
If I find it, I must be
prepared to discuss it in court.

383
00:23:20,933 --> 00:23:22,677
You must, Dr. Forbes.

384
00:23:22,701 --> 00:23:28,572
It's true. The diary expressed
my feelings about my husband,

385
00:23:28,641 --> 00:23:31,808
my marriage, even Dr. Forbes,

386
00:23:31,877 --> 00:23:34,845
and some of those
feelings are fairly intense.

387
00:23:34,913 --> 00:23:39,817
But I would make it
public if it would help you.

388
00:23:39,885 --> 00:23:41,919
I can't ask you to do that.

389
00:23:41,987 --> 00:23:45,121
Then I'll volunteer.

390
00:23:45,190 --> 00:23:46,902
You're always telling me

391
00:23:46,926 --> 00:23:49,593
that I'm not as
fragile as I think I am.

392
00:23:49,662 --> 00:23:54,130
Well, let me prove you're right.

393
00:23:54,200 --> 00:23:59,669
Well, is there anything
incriminating in the diary?

394
00:23:59,738 --> 00:24:01,605
No. Okay.

395
00:24:01,674 --> 00:24:05,176
I, uh, I looked in
your husband's desk

396
00:24:05,244 --> 00:24:06,955
and I couldn't
find it. Where is it?

397
00:24:06,979 --> 00:24:08,645
It's disappeared.

398
00:24:08,714 --> 00:24:11,948
Dora searched his desk,
the library, the house.

399
00:24:12,018 --> 00:24:13,384
It's gone.

400
00:24:13,453 --> 00:24:16,454
Well, that's great.

401
00:24:16,522 --> 00:24:21,024
You both tell me there's
nothing incriminating in it,

402
00:24:21,093 --> 00:24:23,059
but it's gone.

403
00:24:23,129 --> 00:24:25,862
A good prosecutor would
have a field day with this one.

404
00:24:32,838 --> 00:24:35,205
This court will come to order.

405
00:24:36,808 --> 00:24:39,309
What's the delay, counselor?

406
00:24:39,378 --> 00:24:44,348
Your Honor, I'd like to
approach the bench, please.

407
00:24:49,388 --> 00:24:50,788
What's this about, Mr. Burgess?

408
00:24:50,857 --> 00:24:52,389
Your Honor, just
three hours ago,

409
00:24:52,458 --> 00:24:56,093
the state came into
possession of new evidence.

410
00:24:56,162 --> 00:24:57,939
Erin Whitley's
diary. Wait a minute,

411
00:24:57,963 --> 00:25:00,108
Your Honor. Wait a minute.

412
00:25:00,132 --> 00:25:01,477
The defense objects strenuously

413
00:25:01,501 --> 00:25:03,712
to the introduction of
evidence not made available

414
00:25:03,736 --> 00:25:05,948
during the process of discovery.

415
00:25:05,972 --> 00:25:09,706
This court will
recess for 15 minutes.

416
00:25:09,775 --> 00:25:12,442
I'll see you two in my chamber.

417
00:25:12,511 --> 00:25:15,111
Your Honor, at this
stage of the proceedings,

418
00:25:15,180 --> 00:25:17,247
the introduction
of this evidence

419
00:25:17,315 --> 00:25:19,616
is extremely prejudicial
to the defense.

420
00:25:19,685 --> 00:25:21,451
What do you say, counselor?

421
00:25:21,520 --> 00:25:23,331
Your Honor, all
incriminating evidence

422
00:25:23,355 --> 00:25:24,888
is prejudicial to the defense.

423
00:25:24,957 --> 00:25:26,256
Now, procedure is important,

424
00:25:26,325 --> 00:25:30,060
but society's right to justice
is equally as important.

425
00:25:30,129 --> 00:25:32,963
That diary establishes motive.

426
00:25:33,032 --> 00:25:34,965
How do you know it's authentic?

427
00:25:35,034 --> 00:25:37,367
Handwriting expert
John Marshall,

428
00:25:37,436 --> 00:25:39,904
who Mr. Matlock will
recognize as an expert witness,

429
00:25:39,972 --> 00:25:41,052
one you've used before.

430
00:25:43,108 --> 00:25:46,944
He compared handwriting
samples from Mrs. Whitley

431
00:25:47,013 --> 00:25:48,979
to that of the diary,

432
00:25:49,048 --> 00:25:50,993
and he is ready,
absolute ready to testify

433
00:25:51,017 --> 00:25:52,282
to its authenticity.

434
00:25:52,351 --> 00:25:57,154
The defense has also
been searching for this diary.

435
00:25:57,222 --> 00:26:02,659
Now that it's been found,
deserves the time to examine it.

436
00:26:02,727 --> 00:26:06,429
I'll allow defense time
to study the contents,

437
00:26:06,498 --> 00:26:09,767
and we'll resume
again this afternoon.

438
00:26:09,835 --> 00:26:12,602
<i>Call Erin Whitley to the stand.</i>

439
00:26:12,671 --> 00:26:15,772
Mrs. Whitley, do
you recognize this?

440
00:26:15,841 --> 00:26:17,085
Yes.

441
00:26:17,109 --> 00:26:19,475
Will you tell the jury
what it is, please?

442
00:26:19,544 --> 00:26:21,311
It's my diary.

443
00:26:24,950 --> 00:26:26,183
I've marked several passages.

444
00:26:26,251 --> 00:26:28,429
I'd like you to
read the first one

445
00:26:28,453 --> 00:26:30,064
to the court, please.

446
00:26:30,088 --> 00:26:31,288
I object, Your Honor.

447
00:26:31,357 --> 00:26:34,358
The defense is
extremely prejudiced

448
00:26:34,426 --> 00:26:36,471
by the state's last-minute introduction
of this evidence. In addition...

449
00:26:36,495 --> 00:26:37,775
We went thought that

450
00:26:37,829 --> 00:26:39,563
in chambers, Mr. Matlock.

451
00:26:39,632 --> 00:26:42,832
Noted for the
record, but overruled.

452
00:26:42,901 --> 00:26:44,134
Proceed, Mrs. Whitley.

453
00:26:47,439 --> 00:26:50,174
"After last night, I'm
sure Dr. Forbes..."

454
00:26:50,242 --> 00:26:52,802
Excuse me, Mrs.
Whitley. We can't hear you.

455
00:26:57,550 --> 00:27:04,621
"After last night, I'm sure
Dr. Forbes feels the same...

456
00:27:04,690 --> 00:27:07,324
"love for me
that I feel for him.

457
00:27:07,393 --> 00:27:10,894
"Our only obstacle is Adam,

458
00:27:10,963 --> 00:27:13,530
"but Lucas has promised
me that he won't allow Adam

459
00:27:13,598 --> 00:27:14,809
to stand in our way."

460
00:27:14,833 --> 00:27:16,300
I didn't write this.

461
00:27:16,368 --> 00:27:17,379
But this is your diary.

462
00:27:17,403 --> 00:27:19,569
This is your handwriting.

463
00:27:19,638 --> 00:27:21,271
Yes.

464
00:27:21,340 --> 00:27:22,483
Well, then let's go on.

465
00:27:22,507 --> 00:27:24,587
Read the second part
if you would, please.

466
00:27:28,314 --> 00:27:30,414
"I must have Lucas.

467
00:27:30,482 --> 00:27:35,718
"I've loved him from the
first moment I met him;

468
00:27:35,787 --> 00:27:38,221
five days after
that terrible..."

469
00:27:40,426 --> 00:27:42,559
Please continue.

470
00:27:42,627 --> 00:27:44,695
Your Honor, I object.

471
00:27:44,764 --> 00:27:46,830
The prosecution is
harassing a witness

472
00:27:46,899 --> 00:27:48,966
who is under psychiatric care.

473
00:27:49,035 --> 00:27:51,068
Objection overruled.

474
00:27:51,137 --> 00:27:54,171
Please read the passage.

475
00:28:01,213 --> 00:28:04,447
"Five days after
that terrible fire..."

476
00:28:04,516 --> 00:28:12,156
And finally, only the last
one if you would, please.

477
00:28:12,224 --> 00:28:13,568
I didn't write this!

478
00:28:13,592 --> 00:28:18,328
This was written the day
Adam Whitley was murdered.

479
00:28:18,397 --> 00:28:20,530
Please read it, Mrs. Whitley.

480
00:28:24,170 --> 00:28:31,041
"Lucas said that
tomorrow we'll be free."

481
00:28:35,681 --> 00:28:37,881
We've got to talk.

482
00:28:37,950 --> 00:28:40,510
I've made a terrible mistake.

483
00:29:11,750 --> 00:29:12,682
Hello.

484
00:29:12,751 --> 00:29:15,485
Ben, when are you
gonna fire the gun?

485
00:29:15,553 --> 00:29:17,620
I just did. Didn't
you hear anything?

486
00:29:17,690 --> 00:29:19,155
Only the birds chirping.

487
00:29:19,225 --> 00:29:20,957
Huh, that's interesting.

488
00:29:21,026 --> 00:29:24,094
Huh. Okay, okay, thanks.

489
00:29:24,162 --> 00:29:27,697
All I heard was "Keep
breathing. Go for the burn."

490
00:29:27,766 --> 00:29:33,870
Neither Tyler nor you
heard anything. Good.

491
00:29:33,939 --> 00:29:35,572
Glad I could be of some help.

492
00:29:42,014 --> 00:29:44,447
Erin's asleep.

493
00:29:44,516 --> 00:29:46,850
She never moved
when you fired the shot.

494
00:29:46,919 --> 00:29:47,851
Well, you heard 'em.

495
00:29:47,920 --> 00:29:50,520
Yes.

496
00:29:50,589 --> 00:29:51,589
Okay.

497
00:29:51,623 --> 00:29:54,791
I missed it.

498
00:29:58,497 --> 00:30:01,464
I missed it.

499
00:30:01,533 --> 00:30:05,769
It was the child abuse,
it was the extent, I...

500
00:30:05,837 --> 00:30:07,382
We'd just started
to talk about it.

501
00:30:07,406 --> 00:30:09,739
I mean, there were
hints and dreams, but...

502
00:30:09,808 --> 00:30:13,176
I missed it.

503
00:30:13,245 --> 00:30:17,948
Well, I'm... I'm gonna
go ahead with this.

504
00:30:18,016 --> 00:30:19,917
I wish you didn't have to.

505
00:30:19,985 --> 00:30:22,486
You know I do.

506
00:30:26,792 --> 00:30:32,095
Mrs. Whitley, I know
how difficult it must be

507
00:30:32,164 --> 00:30:36,333
for you to testify
in this trial.

508
00:30:36,401 --> 00:30:41,738
So if there's anything I can do
to make it more comfortable...

509
00:30:41,807 --> 00:30:43,607
Thank you, Mr. Matlock.

510
00:30:43,676 --> 00:30:45,275
That's very kind.

511
00:30:45,344 --> 00:30:49,913
You have already testified
that on the night of the murder

512
00:30:49,981 --> 00:30:55,218
you were heavily sedated
and did not hear the gunshots.

513
00:30:55,287 --> 00:30:57,354
That's true. I heard nothing.

514
00:30:57,423 --> 00:30:58,703
So I don't believe it's possible

515
00:30:58,757 --> 00:31:01,758
you could have called
the police, do you?

516
00:31:01,827 --> 00:31:02,870
No.

517
00:31:02,894 --> 00:31:06,896
And, uh, your
housekeeper testified

518
00:31:06,965 --> 00:31:10,300
that she was wearing
one of those tape headsets

519
00:31:10,369 --> 00:31:13,036
and heard nothing and
did not call the police.

520
00:31:13,104 --> 00:31:17,407
If she said so, then it's true.
Dora is absolutely trustworthy.

521
00:31:17,476 --> 00:31:20,744
So no one in the
house called the police.

522
00:31:20,813 --> 00:31:23,347
And I made some
acoustical tests.

523
00:31:23,415 --> 00:31:26,015
And none of the
neighbors heard the shots.

524
00:31:26,084 --> 00:31:29,386
Would you have any idea

525
00:31:29,455 --> 00:31:31,355
who might have
called the police?

526
00:31:31,423 --> 00:31:32,989
No.

527
00:31:33,058 --> 00:31:38,928
So someone else had to have
been in the house that night,

528
00:31:38,997 --> 00:31:45,001
and whoever that someone
was, not only heard the shots,

529
00:31:45,070 --> 00:31:47,337
but fired the shots,

530
00:31:47,406 --> 00:31:50,940
then removed your diary
from your husband's desk

531
00:31:51,009 --> 00:31:53,943
and called the police.

532
00:31:54,012 --> 00:31:58,214
And you have no idea
who might have done that?

533
00:31:58,283 --> 00:32:00,584
I wish I did.

534
00:32:00,652 --> 00:32:02,952
That same person
who did all that,

535
00:32:03,021 --> 00:32:08,492
the killer, then sent
your diary to the police

536
00:32:08,560 --> 00:32:12,929
knowing it would
incriminate Dr. Forbes

537
00:32:12,998 --> 00:32:14,564
and implicate you.

538
00:32:14,633 --> 00:32:16,299
That's correct, isn't it?

539
00:32:16,368 --> 00:32:19,936
I suppose,

540
00:32:20,005 --> 00:32:23,172
but those passages in
my diary, I didn't write them.

541
00:32:23,241 --> 00:32:30,847
Mrs. Whitley, this is
your handwriting, isn't it?

542
00:32:30,916 --> 00:32:32,516
Yes.

543
00:32:32,584 --> 00:32:40,524
Your Honor, I-I ask the court's
permission to re-read a passage

544
00:32:40,592 --> 00:32:43,894
that has already been
read into the record.

545
00:32:43,962 --> 00:32:45,094
I object, Your Honor.

546
00:32:45,163 --> 00:32:46,240
Court's already heard this.

547
00:32:46,264 --> 00:32:51,167
Your Honor, this
is very important.

548
00:32:51,236 --> 00:32:52,947
Objection overruled.
Proceed, Mr. Matlock.

549
00:32:52,971 --> 00:32:54,370
Thank you.

550
00:32:54,440 --> 00:33:02,440
"I must have Lucas. I've
loved him from the first moment

551
00:33:03,081 --> 00:33:10,019
I met him, five days
after that terrible..."

552
00:33:10,088 --> 00:33:13,924
What's that word
right after "terrible"?

553
00:33:13,992 --> 00:33:19,195
Just read that one word.

554
00:33:22,835 --> 00:33:25,001
It's true, isn't it?

555
00:33:25,070 --> 00:33:28,304
That ever since
that awful accident,

556
00:33:28,373 --> 00:33:33,944
you have been unable to speak
or even write the word "fire"?

557
00:33:34,012 --> 00:33:38,682
It takes all that's in you

558
00:33:38,750 --> 00:33:40,116
to be able to hear it.

559
00:33:40,185 --> 00:33:46,356
We need to hear your
response, Mrs. Whitley.

560
00:33:46,424 --> 00:33:49,258
Yes.

561
00:33:49,327 --> 00:33:52,863
And yet here it is in
your diary big as day

562
00:33:52,931 --> 00:33:57,266
the word "fire" written
in your handwriting.

563
00:33:57,335 --> 00:34:01,972
Will you please just read
that word for the court?

564
00:34:07,278 --> 00:34:08,778
I can't!

565
00:34:20,559 --> 00:34:22,336
It's all right, Erin.

566
00:34:22,360 --> 00:34:28,398
I want you to know,
I'm on your side.

567
00:34:28,466 --> 00:34:32,168
This is going to be very hard,

568
00:34:32,237 --> 00:34:34,571
but I'm on your side.

569
00:34:34,640 --> 00:34:38,374
Your Honor, Mr. Matlock
is playing games.

570
00:34:38,443 --> 00:34:41,277
I play games all the
time, Your Honor,

571
00:34:41,346 --> 00:34:43,413
but not when it comes to life.

572
00:34:43,481 --> 00:34:45,493
Mr. Matlock, please continue,

573
00:34:45,517 --> 00:34:47,161
but the court
would like to hear it.

574
00:34:47,185 --> 00:34:50,486
Yes, sir.

575
00:34:50,556 --> 00:34:54,590
Mrs. Whitley, do
you notice my suit?

576
00:34:56,328 --> 00:35:00,763
You notice this smudge
on the arm of my suit?

577
00:35:00,832 --> 00:35:05,134
I wore this suit today for
a very special purpose.

578
00:35:05,204 --> 00:35:09,772
This smudge is caused by makeup.

579
00:35:09,841 --> 00:35:11,474
It is makeup...

580
00:35:11,543 --> 00:35:15,111
A special makeup that's used to
cover blemishes of some kind...

581
00:35:15,180 --> 00:35:18,481
Or... a burn.

582
00:35:21,520 --> 00:35:23,953
Look, look.

583
00:35:24,022 --> 00:35:29,593
It's the same shade as yours.

584
00:35:29,661 --> 00:35:32,195
I mean, on your arm, isn't it?

585
00:35:32,264 --> 00:35:34,063
Yes.

586
00:35:34,132 --> 00:35:36,766
But it didn't come from you.

587
00:35:39,271 --> 00:35:40,849
Your Honor, is there
any point to this?

588
00:35:40,873 --> 00:35:45,541
Your Honor, I know
this is confusing.

589
00:35:45,610 --> 00:35:50,446
I'll tell you, it's the
most confusing case

590
00:35:50,515 --> 00:35:53,283
that's ever come up against me.

591
00:35:53,352 --> 00:35:56,719
It's taken everything
I've got in my mind,

592
00:35:56,788 --> 00:36:01,491
plus expert advice,
opinion, counsel

593
00:36:01,559 --> 00:36:08,198
from several qualified
psychiatrists, to understand it.

594
00:36:08,267 --> 00:36:11,301
Dr. Forbes and I have
discussed what I am about to do.

595
00:36:11,370 --> 00:36:14,371
At first, he thought it
was too dangerous.

596
00:36:14,439 --> 00:36:15,471
I hope not.

597
00:36:15,540 --> 00:36:16,606
I promised him

598
00:36:16,674 --> 00:36:19,642
that, at any point,
he can intercede

599
00:36:19,711 --> 00:36:21,211
and I'll do whatever he says.

600
00:36:21,280 --> 00:36:28,751
The only person who can
clear up all of our confusion

601
00:36:28,820 --> 00:36:34,857
is the person who got
the makeup on my sleeve.

602
00:36:34,927 --> 00:36:39,162
At this point,

603
00:36:39,231 --> 00:36:43,266
I call Shannon
Blackwell to the stand.

604
00:36:46,704 --> 00:36:47,944
Mr. Matlock, procedure requires

605
00:36:47,972 --> 00:36:50,773
that you dismiss one
witness before calling another.

606
00:36:50,842 --> 00:36:52,375
And where is this Ms. Blackwell?

607
00:36:52,444 --> 00:36:55,011
A moment, Your Honor.

608
00:37:08,026 --> 00:37:11,061
Shannon.

609
00:37:11,129 --> 00:37:13,829
Can you hear me?

610
00:37:13,898 --> 00:37:15,932
Shannon.

611
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:19,102
Can you hear me?

612
00:37:19,171 --> 00:37:23,540
Shannon, remember
the first night we met?

613
00:37:23,608 --> 00:37:29,245
You hid from the
headlights of a passing car.

614
00:37:29,314 --> 00:37:33,316
That's when the
makeup on your arm

615
00:37:33,385 --> 00:37:35,552
smudged off on my jacket.

616
00:37:35,620 --> 00:37:39,289
It's the same makeup
that Erin wears.

617
00:37:39,357 --> 00:37:44,561
During that terrible
car crash and fire,

618
00:37:44,629 --> 00:37:48,631
Erin's little dog was killed.

619
00:37:48,700 --> 00:37:51,033
Burned up.

620
00:37:51,103 --> 00:37:53,669
And so was your dog, Shannon.

621
00:37:53,738 --> 00:37:55,405
Burned up.

622
00:37:55,474 --> 00:37:58,874
Erin has many weaknesses,

623
00:37:58,943 --> 00:38:01,611
and though you
don't like to admit it,

624
00:38:01,679 --> 00:38:03,813
so do you.

625
00:38:03,881 --> 00:38:08,985
And somehow this little toy
dog gives you strength, doesn't it?

626
00:38:09,053 --> 00:38:13,055
I went to your
apartment yesterday

627
00:38:13,125 --> 00:38:15,258
and got it for you.

628
00:38:15,327 --> 00:38:17,427
You want it, don't you, Shannon?

629
00:38:26,171 --> 00:38:28,004
Yesterday,

630
00:38:28,072 --> 00:38:32,775
when Erin was
testifying on the stand,

631
00:38:32,844 --> 00:38:39,815
Dr. Forbes realized
for the first time,

632
00:38:39,884 --> 00:38:41,951
there are two of you.

633
00:38:42,020 --> 00:38:44,254
Are you here, Shannon?

634
00:38:46,791 --> 00:38:49,058
You are Shannon, aren't you?

635
00:38:56,400 --> 00:38:59,635
Yes, of course.

636
00:39:04,142 --> 00:39:05,775
And who else?

637
00:39:05,844 --> 00:39:08,811
There's me, just me.

638
00:39:08,880 --> 00:39:12,681
And Erin, and maybe others.

639
00:39:12,751 --> 00:39:15,952
You're a multiple personality,
aren't you, Shannon?

640
00:39:16,020 --> 00:39:17,453
I hate Erin.

641
00:39:17,521 --> 00:39:18,821
She's weak.

642
00:39:18,890 --> 00:39:20,489
She let Adam abuse her.

643
00:39:20,558 --> 00:39:23,159
Well, no one abuses me.

644
00:39:23,228 --> 00:39:26,428
Shannon Blackwell has a future.

645
00:39:26,497 --> 00:39:29,165
Is that why you
killed Adam Whitley

646
00:39:29,234 --> 00:39:32,334
so that you could
start over as Shannon?

647
00:39:32,403 --> 00:39:33,869
I will start over.

648
00:39:33,939 --> 00:39:35,905
Dr. Forbes killed Adam.

649
00:39:35,974 --> 00:39:39,608
Erin was losing
more and more time.

650
00:39:39,677 --> 00:39:42,946
That's because you, Shannon,

651
00:39:43,014 --> 00:39:46,349
were emerging
more and more often.

652
00:39:46,418 --> 00:39:49,919
And sooner or later,
Dr. Forbes would diagnosis

653
00:39:49,987 --> 00:39:52,121
multiple personality.

654
00:39:52,190 --> 00:39:56,526
Dr. Forbes would have destroyed
me to save his precious Erin.

655
00:39:56,594 --> 00:40:00,563
I'm sure he would have
done anything he could

656
00:40:00,631 --> 00:40:04,333
to help both of you.

657
00:40:04,402 --> 00:40:07,903
But you did feel more and
more threatened by Dr. Forbes,

658
00:40:07,972 --> 00:40:09,705
so you did something about it.

659
00:40:09,774 --> 00:40:13,709
You created a little...
a little line of lies.

660
00:40:13,778 --> 00:40:20,049
You put your name and
address in Adam Whitley's rolodex

661
00:40:20,117 --> 00:40:22,552
in your handwriting, which
is different from Erin's.

662
00:40:22,620 --> 00:40:24,320
Yes, it is.

663
00:40:24,389 --> 00:40:27,456
You left messages on
his answering machine

664
00:40:27,525 --> 00:40:29,758
and just days
before he was killed,

665
00:40:29,827 --> 00:40:33,296
you made those
entries in Erin's diary

666
00:40:33,364 --> 00:40:38,100
in<i> her</i> handwriting, which
is different from yours.

667
00:40:38,169 --> 00:40:40,369
You knew it would
cause her trouble.

668
00:40:40,438 --> 00:40:43,306
You hate her so much, Shannon,

669
00:40:43,374 --> 00:40:46,775
that you were hoping she would
collapse under your mischief.

670
00:40:46,844 --> 00:40:49,679
You wanted to be
rid of Erin, rid of her.

671
00:40:49,747 --> 00:40:52,448
You even got your
own apartment...

672
00:40:52,517 --> 00:40:55,918
Created yourself as
"the other woman."

673
00:40:55,986 --> 00:40:57,786
I am stronger than Erin.

674
00:40:57,855 --> 00:40:59,322
I deserve to be free.

675
00:40:59,390 --> 00:41:01,090
Did you hate your father?

676
00:41:01,158 --> 00:41:04,460
He wasn't my father,
he was Erin's father.

677
00:41:04,529 --> 00:41:06,362
No one hits me.

678
00:41:06,431 --> 00:41:07,630
No one beats me.

679
00:41:07,699 --> 00:41:09,131
I'd kill anyone who tried.

680
00:41:09,200 --> 00:41:11,434
He beat her.

681
00:41:11,502 --> 00:41:14,537
She's cry and cry and
crawl off into some corner

682
00:41:14,606 --> 00:41:16,372
and try to hide.

683
00:41:16,441 --> 00:41:21,477
Is that when...
Shannon first emerged?

684
00:41:21,546 --> 00:41:26,149
During those
awful, early beatings

685
00:41:26,217 --> 00:41:30,787
when the weaker Erin
could no longer handle it?

686
00:41:30,855 --> 00:41:35,958
Is that when the stronger
Shannon emerged?

687
00:41:36,027 --> 00:41:38,293
I didn't emerge.

688
00:41:38,362 --> 00:41:39,561
I am.

689
00:41:39,631 --> 00:41:42,498
Shannon...

690
00:41:42,566 --> 00:41:47,036
tell me what happened
the night of the murder.

691
00:41:49,440 --> 00:41:53,275
Dora gave Erin a sleeping pill.

692
00:41:55,312 --> 00:41:56,846
Erin went to sleep.

693
00:41:56,914 --> 00:42:00,116
But you stayed awake.

694
00:42:06,323 --> 00:42:08,390
Uh, I'm going to
tell you something

695
00:42:08,459 --> 00:42:10,860
that you're going to
find hard to believe.

696
00:42:10,928 --> 00:42:13,162
I didn't believe
it for a long time.

697
00:42:13,230 --> 00:42:17,133
In some cases,
a patient suffering

698
00:42:17,201 --> 00:42:19,902
from multiple personalities,

699
00:42:19,971 --> 00:42:23,305
can be given a sleeping pill...

700
00:42:23,374 --> 00:42:27,342
One personality will go to sleep

701
00:42:27,411 --> 00:42:33,949
while the other personality
remains wide awake.

702
00:42:34,018 --> 00:42:38,020
Able to take control
of their mutual body.

703
00:42:38,089 --> 00:42:41,390
Become ambulatory,
walk around, conscious.

704
00:42:43,094 --> 00:42:46,261
I-I know that
seems impossible...

705
00:42:50,768 --> 00:42:55,304
but here is data
of actual cases.

706
00:42:55,372 --> 00:42:58,307
I swear to you it's true.

707
00:42:58,375 --> 00:43:00,542
I enter this as
Defense Exhibit D.

708
00:43:05,016 --> 00:43:13,016
So that night, Erin was asleep
and you were wide awake...

709
00:43:15,326 --> 00:43:18,493
Furious with Adam.

710
00:43:18,562 --> 00:43:22,664
He'd abused Erin just as
her father had abused her.

711
00:43:22,734 --> 00:43:27,369
And your anger
mounted and mounted,

712
00:43:27,438 --> 00:43:31,306
until finally you could
contain it no longer

713
00:43:31,375 --> 00:43:33,575
and you got up, went
downstairs to confront him,

714
00:43:33,611 --> 00:43:36,946
and he-he-he said
something or did something...

715
00:43:37,014 --> 00:43:38,214
He shouted at me

716
00:43:38,282 --> 00:43:40,682
just the way Erin's
father shouted at her.

717
00:43:40,752 --> 00:43:42,718
He was going to hit me.

718
00:43:42,787 --> 00:43:46,155
He was going to take
off his belt and hit me!

719
00:43:46,224 --> 00:43:49,191
So I went into the library
and I got his gun, and I...

720
00:43:51,896 --> 00:43:54,630
and I killed him.

721
00:44:03,141 --> 00:44:09,544
Uh, Your Honor, in light
of these developments,

722
00:44:09,613 --> 00:44:13,883
I move that the case

723
00:44:13,951 --> 00:44:18,821
against Dr. Lucas
Forbes be dismissed.

724
00:44:18,890 --> 00:44:22,024
The prosecution
joins the motion.

725
00:44:22,093 --> 00:44:23,592
Very well.

726
00:44:23,661 --> 00:44:25,795
Motion to dismiss granted.

727
00:44:25,863 --> 00:44:29,564
The court also orders
Shannon Blackwell...

728
00:44:29,633 --> 00:44:31,967
That is Erin Whitley,

729
00:44:32,036 --> 00:44:34,870
held for psychiatric
examination.

730
00:44:34,939 --> 00:44:39,875
Court is adjourned.

731
00:44:39,944 --> 00:44:42,210
Thank you, Mr. Matlock.

732
00:44:42,279 --> 00:44:43,378
Thank you, Doctor.

733
00:44:43,448 --> 00:44:46,008
Excuse me, I have
a patient to see to.

9999
00:00:0,500 --> 00:00:2,00
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
